// Auto-mix: per-frame speaker attribution across N microphones.
//
// The question this answers is "whose mic is the current speaker on", asked
// once per frame, for a set of mics that are EQUAL PARTICIPANTS. There is no
// reference and no target here — that asymmetry belongs to align.js and must
// not leak in, because the driving case is three lavs on three people where
// every mic is someone's close mic and everyone else's bleed.
//
// The discriminator is level PLUS time of arrival. Direct sound arrives first;
// bleed arrives late (~3 ms per metre), quieter and duller. A level-only rule
// (classic Dugan, gain_i = level_i / sum_j level_j) loses a whispered line on
// its own mic to someone else's bleed on a hotter passage, and loses outright
// when recorder trims differ. Timing is the cue that survives both, and it is
// the only cue that carries information while two people talk at once.
//
// WHY THREE TIERS. On separate recorders the lag between two mics is
//
//     measuredLag_ij(t) = clockOffset_ij + drift_ij*t + acousticTDOA_ij(t)
//                         \__ seconds __/  \__ ms __/   \__ +/-3 ms/m __/
//                                                        the entire signal
//
// so the lead/lag sign says nothing until the first two terms are gone. The
// obvious reuse is a trap: buildLattice + solvePath at maxDriftMs 15 would
// absorb the acoustic swing AS drift, because the Viterbi slope penalty exists
// to make a lag series smooth and the non-smooth part is exactly what we want.
// So: a static sync per pair, then an affine clock model fitted in a way that
// provably cannot eat the signal (see fitPairBaseline), then a narrow per-frame
// search around that baseline.
//
// NOT REENTRANT. gccPhat keeps a module-level scratch cache keyed by FFT size
// (gccPhat.js), so the per-pair correlations here must run one at a time.
// Promise.all over pairs would corrupt results silently, with no crash. Real
// parallelism needs worker threads (separate isolates), not async.

const { gccPhat, paddedSlice } = require("./gccPhat.js");
const { estimateStaticOffset, adaptiveGateDb, rmsOf, db } = require("./coarse.js");
const { kWeight, gatedLufs, KWEIGHT_MIN_HZ } = require("./loudness.js");

